WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.816
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.116 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:14.868
Unit twelve: Leadership Theory. Today you will distinguish concepts precisely with whereas / while.

4
00:00:15.168 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.169
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.389
Leadership style.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:29.566
Leadership style means a characteristic way of directing and motivating people.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.067
Her leadership style is collaborative yet decisive.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:36.893
Your turn. Say: Leadership style.

10
00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:41.257
Leadership style.

11
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:43.354
Transformational.

12
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.927
Transformational means inspiring followers to exceed their own expectations.

13
00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:53.072
Transformational leaders connect daily work to a larger purpose.

14
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.336
Your turn. Say: Transformational.

15
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.689
Transformational.

16
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.567
Transactional.

17
00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:07.301
Transactional means based on exchanging rewards for performance.

18
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:11.426
Transactional leadership relies on targets and bonuses.

19
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.379
Your turn. Say: Transactional.

20
00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:18.362
Transactional.

21
00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:20.571
Servant leadership.

22
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:26.323
Servant leadership means leading by prioritising the growth and wellbeing of others.

23
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:30.066
Servant leadership is common in successful NGOs.

24
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.860
Your turn. Say: Servant leadership.

25
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.980
Servant leadership.

26
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:40.008
Vision-casting.

27
00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:44.943
Vision-casting means communicating a compelling picture of the future.

28
00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.838
Vision-casting helped staff see why the reform mattered.

29
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:52.358
Your turn. Say: Vision-casting.

30
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.526
Vision-casting.

31
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.354
Empowerment.

32
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.987
Empowerment means giving people the authority and confidence to act.

33
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:07.278
Empowerment of front-line staff improved customer service.

34
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:10.872
Your turn. Say: Empowerment.

35
00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.827
Empowerment.

36
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:16.840
Accountability.

37
00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.812
Accountability means responsibility for one's actions and results.

38
00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:26.100
Accountability ensures that empowerment does not become chaos.

39
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:29.870
Your turn. Say: Accountability.

40
00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:33.885
Accountability.

41
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.756
Influence.

42
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.433
Influence means the ability to affect others without formal power.

43
00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:44.433
Great leaders exert influence without relying on titles.

44
00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:47.715
Your turn. Say: Influence.

45
00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:51.812
Influence.

46
00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.251
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:57.117 --> 00:03:02.846
Visal, my manager rewards us with bonuses for meeting targets. Isn't that good leadership?

48
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:15.937
It's effective transactional leadership. Transactional leaders exchange rewards for results, whereas transformational leaders inspire people to care about the mission itself.

49
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.132
Which is better?

50
00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:30.356
It depends on the context. While transactional methods work well for routine tasks, transformational leadership tends to drive innovation and loyalty.

51
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.997
And servant leadership?

52
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:43.005
That's different again. Whereas other models focus on organisational goals, servant leadership begins with the growth of the people themselves.

53
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.621
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:46.483 --> 00:03:50.840
Grammar focus: Distinguishing between concepts (whereas and while).

55
00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.361
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:58.486
Transformational leaders inspire, whereas transactional leaders exchange rewards.

57
00:03:59.383 --> 00:04:04.587
While transactional methods suit routine tasks, transformational ones drive innovation.

58
00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:09.526
Servant leaders begin with people, whereas others begin with goals.

59
00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:22.677
'Whereas' and 'while' contrast two parallel facts; they need two complete clauses. 'While' can also mean 'at the same time', so 'whereas' is clearer in formal contrasts. Use a comma before 'whereas' in mid-sentence.

60
00:04:23.417 --> 00:04:28.159
Be careful! Don't say: Whereas X inspire, Y exchanges.

61
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.493
Say: Whereas X inspires, Y exchanges.

62
00:04:33.793 --> 00:04:35.630
Keep subject–verb agreement.

63
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:39.028
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.101
Beyond the Great Man.

65
00:04:41.401 --> 00:04:48.382
Early leadership theory assumed that leaders were born, not made, possessing innate traits that distinguished them from followers.

66
00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:57.520
Later research shifted attention to behaviour, whereas contemporary theories emphasise the relationship between leaders, followers and context.

67
00:04:58.533 --> 00:05:08.892
James MacGregor Burns contrasted transactional leadership, which exchanges rewards for compliance, with transformational leadership, which elevates followers' motivation and values.

68
00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:18.784
Servant leadership, meanwhile, inverts the traditional hierarchy, while situational models argue that no single style suits every circumstance.

69
00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.410
The most effective leaders therefore adapt their approach, while remaining consistent in their underlying values.

70
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:30.560
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:31.417 --> 00:05:33.915
Cats are independent, blank dogs are loyal.

72
00:05:34.215 --> 00:05:38.972
A, whereas. B, despite. C, because.

73
00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:44.719
The answer is A: whereas.

74
00:05:45.883 --> 00:05:49.566
Leadership based on exchanging rewards for performance is blank.

75
00:05:49.866 --> 00:05:53.868
A, transformational. B, transactional. C, servant.

76
00:05:57.433 --> 00:06:00.129
The answer is B: transactional.

77
00:06:01.283 --> 00:06:04.351
Giving people authority and confidence to act is blank.

78
00:06:04.651 --> 00:06:08.827
A, vision-casting. B, accountability. C, empowerment.

79
00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:14.633
The answer is C: empowerment.

80
00:06:15.783 --> 00:06:17.423
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:17.723 --> 00:06:27.321
A, Whereas the first inspires, the second rewards.. B, Whereas the first inspires, but the second rewards.. C, Whereas inspiring, rewards the second..

82
00:06:30.867 --> 00:06:34.770
The answer is A: Whereas the first inspires, the second rewards..

83
00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:39.693
According to the reading, early leadership theory assumed leaders were…

84
00:06:39.993 --> 00:06:45.051
A, made through training. B, born with innate traits. C, chosen by followers.

85
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.517
The answer is B: born with innate traits.

86
00:06:52.733 --> 00:06:55.873
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:56.717 --> 00:07:00.272
What leadership style do you think is most effective, and why?

88
00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:18.549
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:18.849 --> 00:07:51.530
I believe transformational leadership is generally the most effective, particularly in organisations that must innovate. Whereas transactional leadership secures compliance through rewards, transformational leadership inspires people to contribute ideas and effort beyond what is required. However, while an emergency room needs directive leadership, a research team benefits from empowerment. Therefore, the best leaders combine a transformational vision with situational flexibility.

90
00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.748
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:59.984
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and distinguishing between concepts (whereas and while).

92
00:08:00.284 --> 00:08:05.189
Today's value is leadership. Lead fairly, listen to others and set a good example.

93
00:08:05.489 --> 00:08:08.304
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

94
00:08:08.604 --> 00:08:11.384
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

